From: Orin QDMA integration <orin-qdma-dev@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] qdma: preserve escaped recursive make command overrides

MAKEOVERRIDES is an escaped list maintained by GNU make. Applying filter-out
to it splits compiler commands containing spaces and can absorb following
LD, AR and CROSS_COMPILE assignments into CC. Yocto KERNEL_CC carries prefix
mapping flags, so GCC then treats those assignments as input files.

Keep GNU make's original serialization. ARCH is already set with override
in kernel_check.mk; the Yocto recipe unsets userspace CFLAGS/EXTRA_CFLAGS
instead of rewriting the command override list.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/QDMA/linux-kernel/driver/Makefile
+++ b/QDMA/linux-kernel/driver/Makefile
@@ -136,12 +136,9 @@
   export EXTRA_FLAGS
 endif
 
-# Don't allow ARCH to overwrite the modified variable when passed to
-# the sub-makes.
-MAKEOVERRIDES := $(filter-out ARCH=%,$(MAKEOVERRIDES))
-# Don't allow CFLAGS/EXTRA_CFLAGS to clobber definitions in sub-make.
-MAKEOVERRIDES := $(filter-out CFLAGS=%,$(MAKEOVERRIDES))
-MAKEOVERRIDES := $(filter-out EXTRA_CFLAGS=%,$(MAKEOVERRIDES))
+# Preserve GNU make's escaping of command-line values containing spaces.
+# ARCH is already an override in kernel_check.mk. The Yocto caller clears
+# userspace CFLAGS/EXTRA_CFLAGS before invoking this kernel build.
 
 # Exports.
 export grep
